text.section:
Any mutual assessment property and casualty insurer with surplus to policyholders of at least $100,000 may write the following classes of insurance, in addition to those classes enumerated in subsection A of this section:

Water damage insurance as defined in § 38.2-112;


Burglary and theft insurance as defined in § 38.2-113;


Glass insurance as defined in § 38.2-114;


Boiler and machinery insurance as defined in § 38.2-115;


Personal injury liability insurance as defined in § 38.2-117;


Property damage liability insurance as defined in § 38.2-118;


Marine insurance as defined in § 38.2-126;


Home protection insurance as defined in § 38.2-129;


Homeowners insurance as defined in § 38.2-130;


Farmowners insurance as defined in § 38.2-131;


Commercial multi-peril insurance as defined in § 38.2-132; and


Contingent and consequential losses insurance as defined in § 38.2-133.
				The liability coverages specified in this subsection may be written only by insurers having a surplus to policyholders of at least $300,000 unless the coverages are fully reinsured.

Any mutual assessment property and casualty insurer with surplus to policyholders of at least $800,000 may write the following classes of insurance, in addition to those classes enumerated in subsections A and B of this section:

Workers' compensation and employers' liability insurance as defined in § 38.2-119;


Fidelity insurance as defined in § 38.2-120;


Surety insurance as defined in § 38.2-121;


Credit insurance as defined in § 38.2-122;


Motor vehicle insurance as defined in § 38.2-124;


Aircraft insurance as defined in § 38.2-125;


Legal services insurance as defined in § 38.2-127; and


Mortgage guaranty insurance as defined in § 38.2-128.
